\section{The spike study: design, results and localization}\label{sec:S7}

\subsection{The exploratory design}\label{sec:S7.1}

The detection study ran the noise model in the time domain (Table~\ref{tab:S18}). The background moments had a 1/f spectrum, the room field had the cross-spectra of the empty-room recording, and the sensor noise was white. Each component was scaled so that its in-band covariance equaled that of the adult model, and the room field was not projected out. The data were filtered to << F.g4_band_lo_hz >>–<< F.g4_band_hi_hz >> Hz and decimated to << F.meth_td_fs_out_hz >> Hz, with one noise realization per << F.g4_segment_s >>-s segment shared by all arrays. The spike was the spike-wave complex of \citet{hunold2016}, digitized, stretched in time by << F.g4_stretches >> (<< F.g4_n_morphologies >> morphologies) and passed through the same filter.

Spikes were placed at << F.g4_n_locations >> locations stratified by depth below the scalp (<< F.g4_band_10_20mm >>, << F.g4_band_20_30mm >>, << F.g4_band_30_45mm >> and << F.g4_band_45_70mm >> mm; << F.g4_locations_per_band >> locations per band) and by orientation (<< F.g4_n_orientation_bands >> bands from radial to tangential; << F.g4_locations_per_stratum >> locations per depth and orientation stratum). Each location received << F.g4_n_focal_events_per_location >> focal-dipole events, at << F.g4_n_strengths >> strengths of << F.g4_strengths_nam >> nAm, each with every morphology. It also received patch events of << F.g4_patch_radius_mm >> mm radius, which carried the same total moments with the unstretched morphology. This gave << F.g4_n_focal_events >> focal and << F.g4_n_patch_events >> patch events, << F.g4_n_events_per_anatomy >> per anatomy, injected in random order one every << F.g4_event_spacing_s >> s and identically in every array. The adult's locations lay << F.g4_adult_locations_frontal >> in the frontal lobe, << F.g4_adult_locations_parietal >> in the parietal, << F.g4_adult_locations_temporal >> in the temporal, << F.g4_adult_locations_cingulate >> in the cingulate, << F.g4_adult_locations_insula >> in the insula and << F.g4_adult_locations_occipital >> in the occipital lobe, at median depths of << F.g4_adult_median_depth_10_20mm >>, << F.g4_adult_median_depth_20_30mm >>, << F.g4_adult_median_depth_30_45mm >> and << F.g4_adult_median_depth_45_70mm >> mm in the four bands.

Every array was read by two detectors, and Neuromag was also read by its magnetometers alone and by its gradiometers alone, giving << F.g4_n_detectors >> sensor sets per anatomy, each read by both detectors. Both detectors whitened the data with a Ledoit--Wolf covariance \citep{ledoit2004} from << F.g4_null_baseline_minutes >> min of null data and filtered them with the spike templates. The oracle detector knows the source and the time. It tests the whitened, template-filtered projection on the true field pattern at the true peak (one-sided) against a threshold set for a per-trial false-positive probability of << F.g4_oracle_alpha >>.

The practical detector knows neither the source nor the time. At every sample it takes the largest normalized output over the << F.g4_n_morphologies >> templates and << F.g4_n_dictionary_range >> candidate field patterns on a << F.g4_dictionary_spacing_mm >>-mm cortical grid that excludes the true sources. Its local maxima at least << F.g4_refractory_s >> s apart are events. A spike counts as detected when an event above threshold lies within ±<< F.g4_hit_tolerance_ms >> ms of its peak, and the same events are counted as false on null data. The templates are the simulated morphologies and the candidates' field patterns come from the true forward model, which makes the practical detector idealized for every array. Whether it is equally idealized for every array was not tested in the exploratory run; the confirmatory run's mismatch variant tests one departure (Section~\ref{sec:S7.5}), and focal on-scalp patterns may be more sensitive to forward-model and coregistration error.

The practical detector's thresholds for << F.g4_operating_point_per_minute >> false event per minute were set on << F.g4_null_calibration_minutes >> min of independent null data and frozen. On << F.g4_null_heldout_minutes >> min of held-out null data they gave << F.g4_heldout_rate_range >> false events per minute across sensor sets and anatomies (Table~\ref{tab:S9}). In the adult, the practical detector needed << F.g4_adult_practical_over_oracle_s50_10_20mm_range >> times the oracle's strength for half detection at << F.g4_band_10_20mm >> mm.

