S50 is the strength at which the detection rate of a band's focal events reaches << F.g4_s50_level >>, interpolated linearly in log strength between the tested strengths. A band holds << F.g4_n_focal_events_per_band >> focal events: the morphologies pooled over the band's << F.g4_locations_per_band >> locations. The patch events enter neither S50 nor the paired tests. The paired ratio S50\textsubscript{Neuromag}/S50\textsubscript{OPM} is above 1 when the optically pumped magnetometer (OPM) array needs less strength (Section~\ref{sec:S1}). The adult sits at its measured pose and the smaller heads at top contact. The measured pose gives the adult a detectability ratio $D$ << F.g3b_adult_centred_minus_top_d_abs >> dB higher than top contact does, so the adult's spike results are not placed by the same rule as those of the smaller heads.

No exploratory endpoint was named before the analyses. The endpoints, chosen after the analyses, were three. The first was the dense array's detectability ratio against Neuromag's << F.g2_squid_channels >> channels in the adult. The second was Δ of the dense array against the same comparator at top contact in the fixed helmet and in the helmet scaled with the head about the laterally centered head, each against the adult placed by the same rule, reported descriptively. The third, for the spikes, was the dense array against Neuromag's << F.g2_squid_channels >> channels in the << F.g4_band_10_20mm >> mm band with the practical detector. It was tested with the two-sided exact sign-flip test on per-location differences in detection counts, Holm-adjusted \citep{holm1979} over the << F.g4_n_anatomies >> anatomies, with the paired S50 ratio and its location-bootstrap interval as the effect size.

This band, array and detector were chosen from the << F.g4_family_per_opm_array >> comparisons per OPM array of each anatomy, a selection that the correction over anatomies does not control. The detection family has << F.g4_family_per_anatomy >> comparisons per anatomy: two OPM arrays against Neuromag's << F.g2_squid_channels >> channels, its gradiometers and its magnetometers, with both detectors, in << F.g4_n_depth_bands >> depth bands. The localization family has << F.loc_family_per_anatomy >>: two OPM arrays; focal and patch sources at two strengths; and the dipole error, the two errors of dynamic statistical parametric mapping (dSPM), and joint detection and localization with the study's dSPM or with the dipole.

The sign-flip test uses the locations whose difference in detection counts is not zero, and p is smallest when all of them favor one array. With a band's << F.meth_locs_per_band >> locations that smallest p is << F.meth_signflip_min_p_18 >>, and p < << F.meth_alpha >> needs at least << F.meth_signflip_min_n >> such locations. With equal differences the test is the exact sign test. Of << F.meth_locs_per_band >> locations, << F.meth_signtest_18_k >> must then favor one array for p < << F.meth_alpha >> (p = << F.meth_signtest_18_k_p >>; with << F.meth_signtest_18_kminus1 >>, p = << F.meth_signtest_18_kminus1_p >>), and << F.meth_signtest_18_k_holm >> for the first Holm step over << F.meth_n_anatomies >> anatomies, p < << F.meth_holm_first_alpha >> (p = << F.meth_signtest_18_k_holm_p >>). Of the confirmatory << F.meth_confirm_locs >> locations (<< F.meth_confirm_locs_per_stratum >> per orientation stratum), << F.meth_signtest_36_k >> are needed (p = << F.meth_signtest_36_k_p >>) and << F.meth_signtest_36_k_holm >> for the first Holm step (p = << F.meth_signtest_36_k_holm_p >>).

Unequal differences can move p either way: the adult's << F.meth_adult_locs_opm >> locations favoring the OPM against << F.meth_adult_locs_squid >> favoring Neuromag gave p = << F.meth_adult_p >>, against << F.meth_adult_equal_p >> had the differences been equal. Beyond << F.meth_signflip_exact_max >> non-zero locations the run estimated p from << F.meth_signflip_mc_patterns >> random sign patterns (resolution << F.meth_signflip_mc_resolution >>); the p values reported for the confirmatory run are exact (Section~\ref{sec:S7.5}). These values follow from the design alone. Power, and a minimal detectable S50 ratio, depend on how detection varies between locations and were not computed. << F.wr_confirm_pilot_runs_words|capitalize >> pilot runs on test seeds (child A, << F.wr_confirm_pilot_locs_per_band >> locations) gave << F.wr_confirm_pilot_locs >> locations favoring the OPM/Neuromag, p = << F.wr_confirm_pilot_p >>, and their outputs were not kept. The confirmatory declaration describes << F.wr_confirm_pilot_locs_per_band >> locations as underpowered, a reading we do not adopt. The pilot runs prompted doubling the locations to << F.meth_confirm_locs >> but do not estimate power.

\subsection{Results of the exploratory run}\label{sec:S7.2}

The exploratory run had one noise realization per event and an endpoint chosen after the analyses. It is superseded as evidence by the confirmatory run (main text, Section 3.6; Section~\ref{sec:S7.5}) and is reported here in full. In the adult, focal spikes << F.g4_band_10_20mm >> mm below the scalp needed << F.g4_adult_s50_combined_practical_10_20mm >> nAm for half detection with Neuromag's << F.g2_squid_channels >> channels and << F.g4_adult_s50_dense_practical_10_20mm >> nAm with the dense array, a paired S50 ratio of << F.g4_adult_dense_vs_combined_practical_10_20mm_ratio >> << F.g4_adult_dense_vs_combined_practical_10_20mm_ratio_ci >>. Every anatomy's point estimate favored the dense array in this band (S50 ratios << F.g4_all_dense_vs_combined_practical_10_20mm_ratio_range >>; Fig.~\ref{fig:S12}A; Table~\ref{tab:S10}). So did the per-location counts under a Holm correction over the << F.g4_n_anatomies >> anatomies (largest adjusted p << F.g4_holm_10_20mm_max_p_adj >>, child A, whose S50 interval spans 1).

The anatomies are not independent replications, and the correction does not cover the choice of the endpoint from << F.g4_family_per_opm_array >> comparisons per OPM array (below). The site-matched array showed no consistent advantage. The dense array's deeper spikes leaned the same way, with an established difference in only << F.g4_holm_deeper_n_pass >> of << F.g4_deeper_dense_vs_combined_practical_n_cells >> deeper band-and-anatomy cells (Holm within each band; Fig.~\ref{fig:S12}B). The gain lay in the weakest detected spikes.

Table~\ref{tab:S10} gives the superficial band in every anatomy, with the oracle's S50 ratio beside the practical detector's. The oracle is the quantity most directly tied to the detectability metric. Its ratios were larger than the practical detector's in << F.wr_g4_oracle_above_practical_n >> of the << F.g4_n_anatomies >> anatomies (not in the << F.wr_g4_oracle_below_practical_heads >>), as expected where the oracle's advantage is not diluted by the scan over times and candidates. The adult's detection curves are shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:S13}.

