\subsection{Localization}\label{sec:S7.3}

Localization was examined at << F.loc_n_locations >> locations with focal and patch sources of << F.loc_strengths_nam >> nAm, one event per source type and strength at each location (<< F.loc_events_per_condition >> per condition, unstretched morphology), in independent null data. The inverse used a single-compartment boundary-element model (BEM), whereas the simulation used three layers. It also used one of << F.loc_coreg_draws >> coregistration-error draws of << F.loc_coreg_shift_mm >> mm and << F.loc_coreg_angle_deg >>° per location, the same for every array. This error displaced the adult's sources by a median of << F.loc_adult_coreg_displacement_mm >> mm, and by << F.loc_coreg_displacement_mm_range >> mm over the anatomies. The noise covariance was a Ledoit--Wolf estimate from << F.loc_baseline_minutes >> min of null data, and the source grid had fixed orientations at << F.loc_grid_spacing_mm >>-mm spacing (<< F.loc_inverse_grid_range >> sources) and excluded the true source vertices.

Equivalent current dipoles (ECDs) were fitted with MNE-Python \citep{gramfort2013} at least << F.loc_ecd_min_dist_mm >> mm inside the inner skull. dSPM \citep{dale2000}, with depth weighting << F.loc_depth_weighting >> and a regularization set by an assumed signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) of << F.loc_snr >>, was computed in the study's implementation and in MNE-Python's, at the true peak sample. The error is the distance from the true source (a patch's center) to the dipole or to the dSPM peak, read on the MRI through the perturbed transform. Joint success is detection by the practical detector (thresholds from << F.loc_calibration_minutes >> min of null data) with an error of at most << F.loc_joint_threshold_mm >> mm. Paired error differences were tested with the Wilcoxon signed-rank test and joint success with an exact McNemar test.

Both dSPM implementations use fixed orientations on the same grid, the same noise covariance, a depth exponent of << F.meth_dspm_depth >>, $\lambda^{2}$ = << F.meth_dspm_lambda2 >>, a source covariance scaled to the whitened rank and dSPM normalization. They differ in the depth weighting. The study's implementation uses the whitened gains of all of an array's channels, without a limit. MNE-Python's is limited at its default of << F.meth_mne_depth_limit >> and uses the unwhitened gains of the gradiometers, or of the magnetometers where there are none (the OPM arrays). Both are reported, because the paired dSPM differences depend on this choice.

Dipole fits of detected << F.loc_strength_high_nam >>-nAm focal spikes had median errors of << F.loc_ecd_det_focal320_mm_range >> mm in every array and anatomy. Of << F.loc_family_n >> paired comparisons, << F.loc_family_n_sig >> had p < << F.wr_p_exploratory_threshold >>, where << F.loc_family_expected_by_chance >> would be expected by chance. Most of them concerned dSPM errors (<< F.loc_family_n_sig_dspm >> with the study's implementation, << F.loc_family_n_sig_dspm_mne >> with MNE-Python's); << F.loc_family_n_sig_ecd >> concerned dipole errors and << F.loc_family_n_sig_joint_dspm >> joint detection and dSPM localization within << F.loc_joint_threshold_mm >> mm. Of these, << F.loc_family_n_sig_favour_opm >> favored an OPM array, << F.loc_family_n_sig_favour_zero >> had a zero median difference and << F.loc_family_n_sig_favour_squid >> favored Neuromag. Of the << F.loc_family_n_sig >>, << F.loc_family_n_sig_80nam >> concerned mostly undetected << F.loc_strength_low_nam >>-nAm sources, and the two dSPM implementations share their events.

In all, << F.loc_survivors_bonferroni_20 >> comparisons survived a Bonferroni correction within anatomy and array, << F.loc_survivors_bonferroni_20_n_80nam >> of them at << F.loc_strength_low_nam >> nAm, where most sources go undetected, and << F.loc_survivors_bonferroni_all >> survived one over all << F.loc_family_n >>. The adult's dSPM gain for << F.loc_strength_high_nam >>-nAm patches depended on the implementation: << F.loc_adult_dense_vs_combined_patch320_dspm_diff_mm >> mm (p = << F.loc_adult_dense_vs_combined_patch320_dspm_p >>) with the study's estimator and << F.loc_adult_dense_vs_combined_patch320_dspm_mne_diff_mm >> mm (p = << F.loc_adult_dense_vs_combined_patch320_dspm_mne_p >>) with MNE-Python's.

Fig.~\ref{fig:S14} shows every paired error difference with its interval. Of the << F.wr_locfig_n_error_comparisons >> error comparisons, << F.wr_locfig_n_p_below_005 >> had p < << F.wr_p_exploratory_threshold >> (<< F.wr_locfig_n_p_below_005_ecd >> for the dipole fit, << F.wr_locfig_n_p_below_005_dspm_mne >> for MNE-Python's dSPM, << F.wr_locfig_n_p_below_005_dspm >> for the study's). Of these, << F.wr_locfig_n_p_below_bonferroni|words >> fell below << F.wr_locfig_bonferroni_threshold >>, the Bonferroni threshold for the << F.wr_locfig_family_per_anatomy_and_array >> comparisons of one anatomy and OPM array. At << F.loc_strength_high_nam >> nAm the dipole-fit differences lay within a few millimeters of zero in every anatomy, and the dSPM differences were negative or zero. At << F.loc_strength_low_nam >> nAm all << F.wr_locfig_n_open_80nam >> estimates rest mostly on undetected events, whose errors are those of noise, and their intervals are wide.

Of the << F.wr_locfig_n_error_comparisons >> medians, << F.wr_locfig_n_zero_median >> were exactly zero, because the dSPM peaks of both systems often fall on the same vertex of the shared << F.loc_grid_spacing_mm >>-mm grid, and << F.wr_locfig_n_positive_median >> were positive (Neuromag closer). The errors include every event, detected or not, because selecting on detection would select on each system's own noise. Fig.~\ref{fig:S15} gives the share of injected events that each system both detected and localized within << F.loc_joint_threshold_mm >> mm. Of the << F.wr_jointfig_n_mcnemar_per_method >> paired comparisons per method, << F.wr_jointfig_n_mcnemar_below_005_ecd >> with the dipole fit and << F.wr_jointfig_n_mcnemar_below_005_dspm >> with the study's dSPM had p < << F.wr_p_exploratory_threshold >> (exact McNemar, uncorrected), all favoring the OPM array; none survived a correction. Joint success assumes the event time is known, because localization is read at the true peak sample.

Every event received a dipole. Under declared criteria, a dipole or dSPM error above << F.loc_gross_error_threshold_mm >> mm is gross, and a dipole confidence volume above << F.loc_unconstrained_volume_threshold_cm3 >> cm³ is unconstrained. Over the << F.loc_failures_combined_n_events >> events per system, Neuromag had << F.loc_failures_combined_ecd_gross >> gross dipole errors (<< F.loc_failures_combined_ecd_gross_detected >> among its << F.loc_failures_combined_n_detected >> detected events). The dense array had << F.loc_failures_dense_ecd_gross >> (<< F.loc_failures_dense_ecd_gross_detected >> among << F.loc_failures_dense_n_detected >> detected) and the site-matched array << F.loc_failures_matched_ecd_gross >> (<< F.loc_failures_matched_ecd_gross_detected >> among << F.loc_failures_matched_n_detected >>), that is, << F.loc_failures_ecd_gross_rate_detected_range >> of detected events. Gross errors of the study's dSPM among detected events numbered << F.loc_failures_combined_dspm_gross_detected >> for Neuromag (<< F.loc_failures_combined_dspm_gross_rate_detected >>), << F.loc_failures_dense_dspm_gross_detected >> for the dense array (<< F.loc_failures_dense_dspm_gross_rate_detected >>) and << F.loc_failures_matched_dspm_gross_detected >> for the site-matched array (<< F.loc_failures_matched_dspm_gross_rate_detected >>).

Of all gross errors (dipole and the study's dSPM, three arrays), << F.loc_failures_gross_undetected_share >> belonged to undetected events and << F.loc_failures_gross_80nam_share >> to << F.loc_strength_low_nam >>-nAm events. The denominators differ between arrays because each array detects different events, so these rates are described, not compared. The spike study does not test the fitted helmet, so it does not show that fit causes a detection benefit in children. No localization difference was established in any anatomy.

