The confirmatory design was fixed before the run and declared in a configuration file of the code repository (main text, Section 2.5). Its primary result is given in the main text (Section 3.6; Fig. 8) and in Table~\ref{tab:S11}. This subsection gives the declarations in full, the design as run, the Monte Carlo replicates, the realized false-event rates, the mismatch costs, the site-matched array and the results pooled over the replicates.

In Table~\ref{tab:S11}, the dense array's practical-detector columns are the declared endpoint: the dense array against Neuromag's << F.g2_squid_channels >> channels with the practical detector, its thresholds frozen for a nominal << F.cf_operating_point_per_minute >> false event per minute. The other columns are secondary. The oracle columns use the oracle detector, which knows source, waveform and time. The mismatch columns use the declared mismatched detector, with templates between the simulated morphologies, candidate patterns from a single-compartment model with a << F.wr_confirm_coreg_shift_mm >>-mm / << F.wr_confirm_coreg_angle_deg >>° coregistration error and thresholds set for the same rate. The site-matched columns give the site-matched OPM array with the practical detector. The adult sat at its measured head position and the other heads at top contact in the fixed adult helmet; the infant templates are those of \citet{oreilly2021}, from the Neurodevelopmental MRI Database \citep{richards2016}, and children A--C come from OpenNeuro ds005234 \citep{fadeev2024,fadeev2025}.

The declaration fixed seven elements. The seeds derive from a root seed (<< F.meth_seed_confirm_root >>), from which one stream per anatomy and purpose is spawned. The << F.meth_confirm_locs >> locations per anatomy are newly drawn in the << F.g4_band_10_20mm >> mm band (<< F.meth_confirm_locs_per_stratum >> per orientation stratum), vertex-disjoint from the exploratory ones where a stratum allows. The test is the two-sided sign-flip test, exact up to << F.meth_signflip_exact_max >> non-zero location differences and otherwise estimated from << F.meth_signflip_mc_patterns >> random sign patterns. The effect size is the paired S50 ratio with a location-bootstrap interval of << F.meth_boot_confirm >> resamples.

The null data are separate segments for the whitener, for fitting the thresholds, for the held-out check and for a << F.meth_null_evaluation_min >>-min evaluation of the false-event rates of the frozen and the rate-matched thresholds. Each event has << F.rev_seed_confirm_replicates >> noise replicates, the first confirmatory and the others measuring Monte Carlo variability. The mismatched detector has templates at the geometric midpoints between the injected morphologies, candidate patterns from a single-compartment BEM, and a coregistration error of << F.wr_confirm_coreg_shift_mm >> mm and << F.wr_confirm_coreg_angle_deg >>° shared by all arrays.

The run was made at a single code version with the configuration as declared and is complete in all << F.wr_n_anatomies_words >> anatomies. Every random stream was spawned from the root seed << F.cf_root_seed >> by anatomy and purpose (<< F.cf_n_seed_purposes >> purposes), and the noise replicates of an event from its event stream. The exception is the random sign patterns of the sign-flip test, which use the fixed seed << F.rev_seed_signflip_mc >> of the test's implementation in every anatomy, family and replicate (Table~\ref{tab:S17}). The << F.cf_n_locations >> locations per anatomy (<< F.cf_locations_per_stratum >> in each of the << F.cf_n_orientation_strata >> orientation strata) were drawn from pools of << F.cf_stratum_pool_range >> candidate vertices per stratum. The << F.cf_n_exploratory_vertices_excluded >> exploratory locations had been left out of the pools, so that no stratum shares a vertex with the exploratory run.

The nearest exploratory location lay << F.cf_nearest_exploratory_mm >> mm away at the closest and a median << F.cf_nearest_exploratory_median_mm_range >> mm away over the anatomies. The locations' median depth was << F.cf_median_depth_mm_range >> mm; the adult's locations lay << F.cf_adult_locations_frontal >> in the frontal lobe, << F.cf_adult_locations_parietal >> in the parietal, << F.cf_adult_locations_temporal >> in the temporal and << F.cf_adult_locations_occipital >> in the occipital lobe. Each location received << F.cf_n_events_per_location >> focal events per replicate (<< F.cf_n_strengths >> strengths of << F.cf_strength_range >> nAm, morphologies stretched by << F.cf_injected_stretches >>). This gave << F.cf_n_events_per_replicate >> events per replicate, << F.cf_n_events_per_anatomy >> per anatomy over the << F.wr_confirm_replicates_words >> replicates and << F.cf_n_events_total >> in all.

The null data were << F.cf_null_baseline_minutes >> min for the whitener, << F.cf_null_calibration_minutes >> min for the thresholds (<< F.cf_calibration_events_above_threshold >> events above each frozen threshold), << F.cf_null_heldout_minutes >> min held out and << F.cf_null_evaluation_minutes >> min of evaluation null, << F.cf_null_total_minutes >> min in all. The practical detector's dictionary held << F.cf_n_dictionary_range >> candidate patterns over the anatomies. The S50 intervals use << F.cf_bootstrap_resamples >> location resamples. The oracle's realized per-trial false-positive probability on the held-out null was << F.cf_oracle_fpp_range >> over the anatomies and arrays, against the declared << F.cf_oracle_alpha >>.

With more than << F.meth_signflip_exact_max >> non-zero location differences, the run estimated each sign-flip p from << F.cf_sign_flip_n_patterns >> random sign patterns (resolution << F.meth_signflip_mc_resolution >>), and an estimate was zero where no sampled pattern reached the observed statistic. The differences are integer counts, so the exact p over all $2^{n}$ sign patterns follows from the distribution of the signed sum. We computed it from the stored differences for all << F.cf_exact_n_cells >> cells of anatomy and comparison; the << F.cf_exact_n_cells_enumerated >> cells that the run had enumerated itself were reproduced exactly. Every p reported here and in the main text is this exact value. The run's estimates differ from it by at most << F.cf_exact_max_abs_p_diff >> and give the same Holm decision for every anatomy in all << F.cf_exact_n_families >> families. Where an estimate was zero, the exact Holm-adjusted value reaches << F.cf_exact_max_holm_p_where_mc_zero >>.

Before the run, the confirmatory endpoint code was applied to the exploratory run's stored states. It reproduced the exploratory location counts, p values and S50 ratios exactly in all << F.cf_endpoint_code_check_n_comparisons >> comparisons (<< F.wr_n_anatomies_words >> anatomies, both OPM arrays, both detectors).

The mismatch variant's templates sit at the geometric midpoints of the injected stretches (<< F.cf_mismatch_templates >>: << F.cf_mismatch_n_templates >> templates), each injected morphology lying << F.cf_mismatch_template_offset_pct_range >> away from the nearest template. Its candidate patterns come from a << F.cf_mismatch_bem_layers >>-layer BEM. One coregistration error per anatomy (<< F.cf_mismatch_coreg_shift_mm >> mm, << F.cf_mismatch_coreg_angle_deg >>°), shared by all arrays, displaced the candidate dictionary by a median of << F.cf_mismatch_displacement_mm_range >> mm at the spike locations over the anatomies (<< F.cf_mismatch_displacement_locations_mm_range >> mm over all locations). Its thresholds were set for a nominal << F.cf_operating_point_per_minute >> false event per minute on the calibration null and frozen. Like the primary detector's, they were also re-fitted on the held-out null as a secondary analysis.

